## SECTION 11: The Omnibar Quick Command Palette (`Omnibar.tsx` — `Cmd+K` / `Ctrl+K`)

### Screen Location & Visual Focus:
- Centered modal dialog triggered globally by pressing `Ctrl + K` (Windows/Linux) or `Cmd + K` (Mac), or clicking the header search bar.
- Top: Live search input field with instant focus and magnifying glass icon.
- Filter Pills: `All`, `Weak Concepts (<45%)`, `Calculus`, `Linear Algebra`.
- Search Results List: Real-time fuzzy-filtered list of concepts showing concept code, title, subject, current mastery percentage bar, and an `ArrowRight` launch button.
- Bottom Bar: Keyboard navigation helper legend (`↑ ↓ to navigate • Enter to select • Esc to close`).

### Pedagogical & Product Purpose:
High-performing exam students do not want to click through 5 nested menus to find a specific theorem. The Omnibar provides instantaneous keyboard-first access to any topic in the curriculum.

### Presenter Spoken Script:
> "Let me show you one of our most popular power-user features: the **Omnibar Command Palette**. 
> Without touching my mouse, I press `Ctrl + K`. 
> Instantly, a global search overlay appears. I can filter exclusively for my 'Weak Concepts' by clicking this pill, or type 'Chain Rule'. 
> Notice how the results display the real-time Bayesian mastery score right beside the concept title. Pressing 'Enter' transports the student directly into an active adaptive diagnostic session."

### Live Demonstration Action:
- Press `Ctrl + K` on the keyboard to summon the Omnibar.
- Type `Chain` in the input field.
- Use `ArrowDown` to highlight *The Chain Rule for Composite Functions (29% Mastery)*.
- Press `Escape` to close the modal.

### Key Executive Takeaway:
*Reduces navigation latency from 15 seconds to under 1 second, empowering power users and maximizing active study time.*

