## SECTION 12: Hero Banner & "Continue Learning" Spotlight Card (`ContinueLearningCard.tsx`)

### Screen Location & Visual Focus:
- Left column of the top hero grid.
- High-contrast card with deep slate gradients and electric cyan borders.
- Header tags: *"Active Adaptive Diagnostic"* and *"Syllabus Sprint 2026"*.
- Prominent Title: *"The Chain Rule for Composite Functions"*.
- Metadata: Subject (*Calculus I*), Chapter (*Derivatives & Tangents*), Difficulty (*Advanced*), Estimated Time (*12 mins*).
- Primary Button: Glowing blue-cyan `Resume Learning` button with an arrow icon.

### Pedagogical & Product Purpose:
Completely eliminates **decision fatigue**. When students open a learning app and are forced to decide what to study, 40% abandon the session. The spotlight card uses our BKT algorithm to calculate the single highest-yield concept that the student needs to practice *right now*.

### Presenter Spoken Script:
> "When a student sits down to study, the hardest part is often deciding where to start. 
> Our dashboard eliminates that friction entirely through this 'Continue Learning' spotlight card. 
> The system has scanned Alex's knowledge profile and determined that 'The Chain Rule' is his highest-leverage remediation point. With a single click on 'Resume Learning', he is immediately engaged in an active problem."

### Live Demonstration Action:
- Point out the 'Estimated Time: 12 mins' tag — explain how bite-sized micro-sessions lower psychological resistance to studying.

