## SECTION 13: The Flagship 3D Knowledge Galaxy Orb (`KnowledgeGalaxy.tsx` / `KnowledgeOrb.tsx`)

### Screen Location & Visual Focus:
- Right column of the top hero grid (occupies 6 of 12 columns).
- Fully rendered interactive 3D WebGL Canvas displaying the student's personal knowledge universe.
- Multiple concentric orbital rings populated with revolving concept spheres:
  - **Emerald Green Spheres:** High mastery ($\ge 75\%$) — e.g., Limits, Basic Derivatives.
  - **Electric Blue Spheres:** Moderate mastery ($40\% - 74\%$) — e.g., Definite Integrals.
  - **Rose Red Spheres:** High-risk knowledge gaps ($< 40\%$) — e.g., Chain Rule, Integration by Parts.
- Interactive HUD Overlay:
  - Play / Pause orbit animation button.
  - Zoom In (`+`) and Zoom Out (`-`) controls.
  - Reset View button.
  - Floating Concept Info Card that appears when hovering or clicking any node, displaying concept title, subject, mastery percentage, and prerequisite dependencies.

### Pedagogical & Product Purpose:
Provides **gestalt visual comprehension** of academic readiness. Instead of scanning a 50-row spreadsheet, a student or teacher immediately sees which areas of the universe are glowing green versus which clusters are dim and red.

### Presenter Spoken Script:
> "Next to the spotlight card is our flagship visualizer: the **3D Knowledge Galaxy**. 
> This is not a static illustration; it is an interactive physics-driven visualization of the student's mind. 
> Look at the inner orbit: 'Limits & Asymptotes' is glowing bright green with 92% mastery. 
> But look out at this outer orbit: 'The Chain Rule' is glowing rose-red with 38% mastery. 
> Let me click on this node. Notice how our HUD overlay immediately locks onto the concept, showing its exact Bayesian mastery, its prerequisite trail, and a one-click button to practice it immediately."

### Live Demonstration Action:
- Click and drag inside the canvas to pitch and yaw the 3D orbit.
- Click the `Pause` button to freeze the orbital movement.
- Click directly on 'The Chain Rule' node to open the HUD card.
- Click `Resume Orbit`.

### Key Executive Takeaway:
*Unprecedented visual engagement: turns an intimidating exam syllabus into an exploratory, conquerable galaxy.*

